## Balance: the predicted win-rate spread of the decks each cube produces

Every deck the cube produced in the data, against the cube's other decks (at most 400 of them), play and draw averaged; the SD across decks in win-rate points. **SD** is de-biased for shrinkage (D342): sqrt of the mean, over 200 draws from M1's Laplace posterior, of the squared SD, with the 2.5-97.5% of the draws as its interval. **Shrunk** is the old number, the SD of the MAP's predictions, which is biased toward "balanced" by an amount that depends on the games a cube has. **Reliability** = shrunk^2 / SD^2, the share of the spread the data has pinned down: **compare two cubes only when their reliabilities are alike** -- otherwise the ranking is partly a ranking by sample size.

| cube | decks | SD (points) | 95% interval | shrunk | reliability | a deck's posterior SD | best deck | worst deck |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| fair-fight | 11490 | 7.6 | 7.1-8.1 | 6.9 | 0.83 | 3.2 | 74.1% | 27.2% |
| modern-era | 11562 | 8.7 | 8.1-9.2 | 8.1 | 0.88 | 3.2 | 75.4% | 24.4% |
| omega | 10428 | 6.4 | 5.8-6.9 | 5.5 | 0.75 | 3.3 | 70.5% | 31.7% |
| pauper | 16628 | 8.3 | 7.8-8.7 | 7.8 | 0.88 | 3.0 | 76.8% | 20.6% |
